# Creating a skill

When the user asks to **create / add / install / author a skill**, or when you
are about to write a new `SKILL.md` or `ln -s` a skill into a personal skills
directory, treat `engine/skills/create-skill/SKILL.md` as the source of truth.

**First action:** Read the installed `create-skill` skill
(`~/.cursor/engine/skills/create-skill/SKILL.md`, `~/.claude/engine/skills/create-skill/SKILL.md`,
or `~/.codex/engine/skills/create-skill/SKILL.md` after `./install.sh`) or
`engine/skills/create-skill/SKILL.md`.

## Invariants (assert)

- A skill MUST apply to **Claude, Cursor, Codex, and Muse** unless it is listed in
  `CLAUDE_ONLY_SKILLS` in `install.sh`.
- Prefer `product/skills/<name>/` (or `corpus/skills/<name>/`) in catstack + `./install.sh`.
- Project-skill home links MUST use all four roots (or
  `scripts/install/link_skill_three_harnesses.sh`) — never a subset.
- After install/link, run `python3 scripts/ci/check_skills_three_harnesses.py`
  (add `--home` when checking live personal roots).

Do not follow Cursor built-in create-skill advice that only mentions
`~/.cursor/skills/`. Do not leave any harness root unlinked.

Incident this prevents: agents home-linked `wipe-bad-pr` into Claude and
Cursor only and missed `~/.codex/skills/`.
